# Copy to .env.local (dev) or set in your host's dashboard. Every key is optional:
# without any of them the app runs on keyless public sources and the built-in quant engine.

# --- AI analysis & market brief -------------------------------------------------------------
# Without any AI key the built-in quant engine writes the analysis. With keys, models are tried in
# order; a model that is rate-limited, retired or returns bad JSON is skipped for a while and the
# next one is used, ending with the quant engine. Settings -> AI analysis shows the live chain.

# OpenRouter (default, free models): https://openrouter.ai/keys
# Free models allow 20 requests/min and 50/day (1000/day once $10 of credit has ever been bought).
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Preferred model(s), comma-separated, tried before the fallback list. Applies to the primary provider.
# AI_MODEL=minimax/minimax-m3.1-flash:free
# Replace the built-in fallback list (comma-separated). Current free list (Oct 2026):
# AI_FALLBACK_MODELS=minimax/minimax-m3.1-flash:free,nvidia/nemotron-3.5-super-vl:free,thinkingmachines/inkling:free,google/gemma-4-31b-it:free,nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b:free,openrouter/free
# Primary provider when several keys are set: openrouter | gemini | groq | custom | openai
# AI_PROVIDER=openrouter

# Alternatives. Every configured provider joins the chain after the primary one.
# Google Gemini (free tier): https://aistudio.google.com/apikey  -> gemini-flash-latest
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# Groq (free tier): https://console.groq.com/keys  -> openai/gpt-oss-120b, llama-3.3-70b-versatile
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# OpenAI (paid): https://platform.openai.com/api-keys  -> gpt-5-mini
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# Any other OpenAI-compatible endpoint; models come from AI_MODEL (set AI_PROVIDER=custom to make it primary).
# Example, OpenCode Zen paid models: AI_BASE_URL=https://opencode.ai/zen/v1 (its free models only work inside the OpenCode app)
# AI_API_KEY=
# AI_BASE_URL=

# --- Market data (all optional) ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Finnhub free tier, used as a backup for quotes, company news and earnings if Yahoo is blocked:
# https://finnhub.io/register
# FINNHUB_API_KEY=

# FRED API key raises rate limits for macro indicators (keyless CSV is used otherwise):
# https://fredaccount.stlouisfed.org/apikeys
# FRED_API_KEY=

# CoinGecko demo key for higher crypto rate limits: https://www.coingecko.com/en/developers/dashboard
# COINGECKO_API_KEY=

# --- Hosting -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Canonical URL: used for metadata, robots.txt and the www -> apex redirect.
# SITE_URL=https://stockanalyses.org
# Set to "fetch" to skip the Chrome-impersonating HTTP client (impit). It falls back to plain fetch
# automatically if its native binary cannot load; Yahoo usually rate-limits plain fetch from cloud IPs.
# HTTP_CLIENT=
